      "value": "@{5a02a34ac6f7657d596cd51f|full_name}: No they do nothing. Some things are allowed to change or show changes in Unity but in fact do nothing when put into VRChat like Rigid Bodys, cameras (just recently), or certain body part animations, like I can only move up and down using the Transform Position.y and not the Animator.Root T which also means that because  of being forced to use Transform Position.y I some reason also can't even bend over which makes no sense to how that even works. Despite what Darkvulpine suggest changing between sit and stand also does nothing for me. Sometimes it won't even let me change a Transform due to the avatar being called humanoid or not even though I set all my avatars up the same which is annoying because Animator.Root T doesn't effect walking animations in VRChat. They really need to make it so the View Position changes with the head/eyes actual position therefore have an attachable bone option the same way you attach another other mesh or object to the Avatar. But as I say have it optional and/or only for the y axis due to emotes or pick the axes the uploaded Avatar can change. Or simple just disabled for individually specified emotes in the AvatarControllerTemplate. There's so many ways to improve or change it than what it is now. I almost don't even bother sitting down anymore.\n\nWith my floating characters, because the view position stays and my whole body and head moves, my arms stay in a fixed position in the world and you can never be sure with where your body parts are unless you look down or have a mirror which is weird enough if your Avatar isn't using perfect typical Human shaped bones. I really see no reason for having things fixed or limited when the uploader of the avatar's get to pick how it animates and smoothly it works. I spend hours and care for my models. I am very passionate about them unlike most basic Avatars that are generic as hell. It just makes no sense right now and breaks immersion. It's already bad enough with the immersion due to all the non-VR users and Knuckles. Like is it really too much to want my own avatars to at least function properly instead of making me scroll through an extra 20+ avatars than I am meant to, just to change each little action I do due to the View Position and transforms being different?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
