  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Right now if I make a new walking animation that makes an Avatar's vertical position change for flying/floating up and down or size transforming then the view position should change with it or allow it to be changed via animations. Or allow View Position to be attached to a bone of our choice. Like in the script, allow a search for that bone.\n\nThis should also fix the sitting down problem I experience a lot of the time that has the View Position too high and forces my hands to be raised in the air. This way the View Position will stick with where the Head/Eyes actually are.\n\nEdit: This should be added as something optional just like how you can pick to use visemes or not. And it would make for a better immersion for unique avatars that aren't generic humans or static models.",
